    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n77673" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάντοτε</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>always</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philem.
				187
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1166a28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				<u>Mon.</u>
				324
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				720
			</span></i>; twice in <i><span class="en">LXX,
				<u>Wi.</u>11.21</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				19.18
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				1123.8
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i B. C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
				26.11
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				3.1362
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.2713
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.Chr.
				32.37
			</span></i>, etc.: condemned by  the Atticists, who
			recommend <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαπαντός</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑκάστοτε</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
				82
			</span></i>, Moer.<i><span class="en">
				p.319
			</span></i> P.</div>
